Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0005.
Two hooks so a quantization plugin can serve DeepSeek-V4.1's dense linears in a non-FP8 format (the recipe's
vllm_exl3_moe plugin: EXL3 trellis wq_b / wo_a / wo_b / shared expert, ~5 bits per weight against MXFP8's 8.25; the
dense FP8 linears are ~34% of a TP=2 decode step on GB10 and bandwidth-bound):
1. deep_gemm_fp8_o_proj: if wo_a carries `grouped_bmm` (o_rot [tokens, groups, K] -> [tokens, groups, N]), run the
   inverse RoPE unquantized and hand the groups to it, before the SM12x Marlin and FP8 paths.
2. _pad_shared_expert_weight: leave tensors without the intermediate axis (sign vectors, scalars) alone instead of
   indexing a dimension they do not have. Both are no-ops for the checkpoint's own FP8 tensors.

